# The DOMUS improvement loop keeps its round-by-round record here: what was
# tried, what was measured, and — more usefully — what was measured and
# reverted. That history is worth keeping in the repo.
#
# Its raw sweep logs are not. Each `ORTHO_TEST_DEBUG` run emits 100-160MB of
# fixture geometry and there are dozens of them, ~3.9GB in total; GitHub
# rejects any single file over 100MB, and git history is permanent. Only the
# distilled results are tracked.
!.tmp/domus-improve/
.tmp/domus-improve/*.log
.fallow/
test-results/
.playwright-mcp/
